From 4c5f06eb018f4e0b85f71b6335ad19ef9a66f828 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler South <tsouth2@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 19:39:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Mute Hyprland's sound for every terminal bell

Hyprland 0.57 plays a sound for each xdg-system-bell ring, and Foot rings it
on a missed Tab completion, Backspace at an empty prompt and other routine
keys. Each sound opens the Windows audio device through QEMU. Where that open
fails, the VM stalls and the launcher reports the desktop as unresponsive
(#384).

Backport Omarchy's fix (basecamp/omarchy c019850d), which sets bell_sound to
none. Hyprland 0.56 rejects the unknown option, so set it only on 0.57 and
later. The change is in default/, which is now listed as a backported tree.
Runtime 4.0.4-12 brings it to existing disks with the next Update > Omarchy.
